+/// Reuses every paragraph whose bytes provably match between `old_text` and `new_text` -- because
+/// it lies entirely within their common byte prefix or suffix -- and reshapes only what's left in
+/// between. A single-character edit therefore reshapes exactly one paragraph instead of the whole
